@startuml signal-correlation
title US-06: Signal Correlation - Proximity candidate triggers composite if signal loss found; one composite per episode

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nproximity.candidates" as ProxKafka
participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
database "Redis\nalert-state:{id}" as AlertState
database "Redis\nrecent-loss:{id}" as RecentLoss
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j

note over Evaluator
  Runs on Kafka consume from proximity.candidates.
  Only the elected leader evaluates.
  SIGNAL_LOSS was already emitted when entity went dark.
  If proximity arrives within the correlation window,
  the SIGNAL_LOSS is superseded — not suppressed.
  Each signal-loss episode can produce at most one COMPOSITE.
end note

ProxKafka -> Evaluator : consume proximity.candidates event\n{ pair_key, entity_a_id, entity_b_id,\n  episode_start_ms, lat, lon, distance_at_detection }

note over Evaluator
  Check each entity for an active or recent signal loss.
  Known associates already filtered upstream.
end note

Evaluator -> AlertState : HGETALL alert-state:{entity_a_id}
AlertState --> Evaluator : { dark_since_ms, signal_loss_alert_id, composite_issued } or nil

Evaluator -> AlertState : HGETALL alert-state:{entity_b_id}
AlertState --> Evaluator : { dark_since_ms, signal_loss_alert_id, composite_issued } or nil

alt active signal loss found AND composite_issued == 0
  note over Evaluator
    Entity is currently dark and no composite issued yet.
    alert-state provides dark_since_ms and signal_loss_alert_id.
    Check that proximity episode_start_ms falls
    within COMPOSITE_CORRELATION_WINDOW_MS of dark_since_ms.
  end note

  Evaluator -> Neo4j : targeted lookup for proximity episode context
  Neo4j --> Evaluator : episode context confirmed

  Evaluator -> AlertState : set composite_issued = 1
  Evaluator -> Evaluator : -> composite emission\n(see composite-emission diagram)

else no active signal loss — check recent-loss window
  Evaluator -> RecentLoss : HGETALL recent-loss:{entity_a_id}
  RecentLoss --> Evaluator : { dark_since_ms, resumed_at_ms, signal_loss_alert_id }\nor nil (expires after COMPOSITE_CORRELATION_WINDOW_MS)

  Evaluator -> RecentLoss : HGETALL recent-loss:{entity_b_id}
  RecentLoss --> Evaluator : { dark_since_ms, resumed_at_ms, signal_loss_alert_id } or nil

  note over RecentLoss
    Entity resumed broadcasting but was dark recently.
    Position Consumer wrote recent-loss before deleting alert-state.
    Key expires after COMPOSITE_CORRELATION_WINDOW_MS.
    Its presence means the correlation opportunity is still open.
  end note

  alt recent-loss found AND episode_start_ms within window of resumed_at_ms
    Evaluator -> Neo4j : targeted lookup for proximity episode context
    Neo4j --> Evaluator : episode context confirmed

    Evaluator -> RecentLoss : DEL recent-loss:{entity_id}

    note over RecentLoss
      DEL consumes the correlation opportunity.
      Subsequent proximity events for this entity
      find no recent-loss and produce UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY
      as independent incidents — not further composites.
    end note

    Evaluator -> Evaluator : -> composite emission\n(see composite-emission diagram)

  else no qualifying signal loss for either entity
    Evaluator -> Evaluator : emit UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY alert
  end
end

@enduml
